ART AND REGISTRATION
Camera: orthographic, elevation 35.2643897 degrees, azimuth 45 degrees.
World: right-handed XZ ground, Y up. Source density 440 px per metre.
Canvas: 1536 square. Common ground root: [768, 1220].

Front-elevation illustrated masters supply the door, masonry portals and moving
mechanical surfaces. Authored contour depth supports the masonry. The lever
pedestal, valve body and bell volume have additional freshly illustrated
isometric masters. The winch barrel uses the same rope painting wrapped on a
curved surface; the lever grip uses an axial billboard around a fixed world
hinge so a round handle does not collapse edge-on during its swing.

Broken states use editable clipping meshes and rigid source fragments; masters
are never overwritten. Selected exposed raw wood/metal faces are source-authored.
No animation frame was independently regenerated. No alpha thresholding, grain
or texture filters are applied. Some raw viewers show RGB beneath transparent
pixels; composited proof surfaces are the reliable alpha preview.

FUNCTIONAL CONTRACTS
Door: fixed left hinge, 100-degree swing.
Portcullis: 2.08 m upward travel into an opaque overhead shaft, clipped above
world y=2.08. An overhead shaft is still required in the scene.
Lever: 70-degree throw around its source-registered axle.
Pressure plate: 0.08 m vertical depression.
Valve: wheel rotates on its fixed spindle between static endpoint states.
Winch: crank rotates about its fixed drum axle. Symmetric fully wrapped drum
appearance is invariant between the two static states.
Bell: shell and clapper swing from a fixed mount; broken shell loses a cast
fragment and clapper.
Crypt seal: 1.27 m downward slab travel into the sill, geometrically occluded
below its threshold. Static open state matches the original travel amount.

KNOWN LIMITS / INTEGRATION
This is hand-illustrated 2.5D art, not a relightable 3D asset pack. Source-baked
lighting follows moving surfaces. The door's reverse shares its front artwork.
The bell is a volumetrically painted cutout on a fixed-camera skeletal rig.
New silhouettes differ from the original blockouts: engine colliders and bounds
need review. No engine import, gameplay collision or runtime timing is claimed.
Root visual gate passed. Registered source geometry uses the exact camera matrix; generated isometric volumes are fixed-view illustrations with artistic internal perspective, not calibrated 3D meshes. Asset IDs, state names, original clip IDs, canvas and root are preserved. Engine collision review remains required.

R02A SOURCE-PORTABILITY REPAIR (6 October 2026)
Only source usability/documentation changed. Every previously delivered artwork,
master, still, frame, layer, atlas and review image/movie is byte-identical to r02.
The eight images in source/historical_before/ are unchanged original comparison
inputs, not additional designs or runtime assets. They make package_proof.py
